    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.03) and **Trevor Story** (69.17), both of whom offer the highest efficiency floors. **Trevor Story** benefits from a distinct park boost and a favorable matchup against the right-handed arm of Rodriguez, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** captures the top spot due to a massive 14% platoon edge against Law, putting him in a premium position to drive in runs from the three-hole. **Seiya Suzuki** (64.25) also warrants attention; he draws a favorable matchup against Gasser and gains a boost from a slow-delivering pitcher that should facilitate an opportunistic stolen base attempt, a critical component given our emphasis on the scarcest category.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal range of our bench. **Zach McKinstry** (40.62) and **Austin Riley** (41.42) barely held their spots, primarily because their matchups against tough arms like Ryan and Luzardo suppressed their ceiling. While **Austin Riley** carries a respectable pedigree, the combination of a low batting order position and a deep-seated SP skill disadvantage effectively neutralized his potential. We opted to stay the course with the current starters, as no player on our bench\u2014including **Corbin Carroll**, who is currently listed as a DNP/Rest\u2014offers the requisite combination of active status and favorable platoon alignment to displace the bottom of our lineup. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **James Wood** (48.76) and **Max Muncy** (45.96) facing elite pitchers in Pivetta and Cease, respectively. Both are forced into the lineup by virtue of their xwOBA metrics, but their scores are significantly depressed by the opposing SPs' ability to limit production. We are closely monitoring weather reports for any late-breaking shifts that might affect these matchups, but as it stands, we are banking on the high-leverage spots of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Griffin Conine** to provide the necessary run production to sustain our 5x5 standing against the league leaders.",
